course: dictionary
lesson: 7004
title: A paramecium
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A paramecium is a tiny living thing that lives in ponds and fresh water. It is far too small for your eyes alone, so you need a microscope to see it.
explain: It is made of just one cell, yet it does everything a living thing needs. It moves, and it eats bacteria. Scientists call a living thing like this a single-celled organism.
explain: The sentence says: «Put one drop of pond water under a school microscope and a whole hidden world swims into view: slipper-shaped paramecia rowing with tiny hairs.» The clues tell you its shape is like a slipper, and it moves by rowing with hairs.
fact: A paramecium is a single-celled organism, which means its whole body is one cell.
fact: «Paramecia» is the plural of paramecium, so one paramecium means many paramecia.
fact: A paramecium is shaped like a slipper and moves by beating thousands of tiny hairs called cilia.
fact: Paramecia live in ponds and fresh water, and you can only see them with a microscope.
fact: A paramecium eats bacteria, which are also tiny living things.
exercise: «Put one drop of pond water under a school microscope and a whole hidden world swims into view.» What do you need to see a paramecium? | A torch | A pair of binoculars | *A microscope | A telescope
exercise: A paramecium is a single-celled organism. What does single-celled mean? | It has a hundred cells | It is made of plant leaves | It has no cells at all | *Its whole body is one cell
exercise: How does a paramecium move? | *By beating thousands of tiny hairs called cilia | It flies with wings | It slides along on a fixed stalk | It grows roots and stays still
test: Where does a paramecium live? | Only inside a computer | In a desert with no water | *In ponds and fresh water | On the tops of mountains
test: What shape is a paramecium? | *Shaped like a slipper | A long thin worm | A ball like a football | A flat square
exam: Which sentence best describes a paramecium? | It is a plant with roots and leaves | *It is a tiny living thing made of one cell that you need a microscope to see | It is a large animal you can see from across a field | It is a stone that floats on ponds
